{"nodes": [{"id": "context_count", "label": "Count (glossary)", "file_type": "concept", "rationale": "The servo encoder's unit of absolute position; 4096 per servo turn. Avoid: tick, step, encoder unit.", "source_file": "CONTEXT.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "context_output_degree", "label": "Output Degree (glossary)", "file_type": "concept", "rationale": "An angle measured at the mechanism after the 44:30 belt reduction; one count is 0.06 output degrees. Unqualified 'degrees' always means output degrees. Avoid: servo degree, which is the pre-belt angle and a different quantity.", "source_file": "CONTEXT.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "context_datum", "label": "Datum (glossary)", "file_type": "concept", "rationale": "The calibration reference captured from a real servo reading, against which output angles are measured. Must sit mid-travel; a datum at count 0 strands the negative half. Avoid: zero point, home, origin, offset.", "source_file": "CONTEXT.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "context_zero_reference", "label": "Zero Reference (glossary)", "file_type": "concept", "rationale": "A saved, named baseline position an operator can recall. The datum is one distinguished zero reference, not a separate kind of thing. Avoid: preset, bookmark, waypoint.", "source_file": "CONTEXT.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "context_travel_window", "label": "Travel Window (glossary)", "file_type": "concept", "rationale": "The reachable output-angle range, plus/minus 90 degrees by default. A target outside it is refused as out_of_travel, never clamped. 180 degrees of output is 3004 counts, inside one servo turn. Avoid: range, limits, bounds.", "source_file": "CONTEXT.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "context_snapshot", "label": "Snapshot (glossary)", "file_type": "concept", "rationale": "One instantaneous sensory readout from the servo, carrying its own valid flag. An invalid snapshot is a failed read, not a reading of zero. Avoid: reading, poll, sample.", "source_file": "CONTEXT.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "context_sample", "label": "Sample (glossary)", "file_type": "concept", "rationale": "One persisted telemetry row, written by the sampler at the configured interval and subject to retention. Avoid: snapshot, record, datapoint.", "source_file": "CONTEXT.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "context_fault", "label": "Fault (glossary)", "file_type": "concept", "rationale": "One of six conditions decoded from status register 0x41: overload, overcurrent, overheat, voltage, sensor, angle. Avoid: error; alarm is the UI's word for a surfaced fault.", "source_file": "CONTEXT.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "context_timestamp_term", "label": "timestamp (glossary)", "file_type": "concept", "rationale": "The time field on every entity, schema, DB column, CSV column and query param, spelled out everywhere. Avoid: ts, time, when.", "source_file": "CONTEXT.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "context_bridge", "label": "Bridge (glossary)", "file_type": "concept", "rationale": "The RPC channel between the Linux side and the MCU. Calls are serialised; payloads are CSV strings with typed arguments. Avoid: link, IPC, channel.", "source_file": "CONTEXT.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "context_relay", "label": "Relay (glossary)", "file_type": "concept", "rationale": "The MCU-side byte pump that mirrors Ethernet-shield connections to the Linux side. Owns no HTTP knowledge; it moves bytes. Avoid: proxy, tunnel, forwarder.", "source_file": "CONTEXT.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "context_slot", "label": "Slot (glossary)", "file_type": "concept", "rationale": "One mirrored TCP connection inside the relay, identified by index, adopted exactly once via accept(). Avoid: socket, connection id, channel.", "source_file": "CONTEXT.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "context_lock", "label": "Lock (glossary)", "file_type": "concept", "rationale": "The digital interlock that refuses movement while engaged. Avoid: e-stop, freeze, hold, safety.", "source_file": "CONTEXT.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "context_backend", "label": "Backend (glossary)", "file_type": "concept", "rationale": "Which ServoRepository implementation is live, simulated or hardware, selected by use_hardware_servo. Avoid: mode, driver, mock, fake.", "source_file": "CONTEXT.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "context_ubiquitous_language", "label": "Ubiquitous Language Glossary", "file_type": "rationale", "rationale": "CONTEXT.md carries a Language section defining the project's domain terms with explicit Avoid lists, so issue titles, test names and proposals use one vocabulary. Maintained by the domain-modeling skill.", "source_file": "CONTEXT.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "context_air_gapped_deployment", "label": "Air-Gapped Deployment", "file_type": "rationale", "rationale": "Final deployment is air-gapped; the dev board has WiFi, production ones will not. Develop as if already air-gapped so shipping is 'zip the folder'. Drives the no-framework, no-bricks, vendored-libraries and wheelhouse decisions.", "source_file": "CONTEXT.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "context_no_framework", "label": "Plain HTML/CSS/JS, No Framework", "file_type": "rationale", "rationale": "Air-gap: there is no build pipeline to vendor.", "source_file": "CONTEXT.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "context_lcars_theme", "label": "LCARS Light Theme With ISA-101 Safety Colours", "file_type": "rationale", "rationale": "Chosen after many iterations.", "source_file": "CONTEXT.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "context_typed_inputs", "label": "Typed Inputs, Not Sliders", "file_type": "rationale", "rationale": "Operators need exact angles.", "source_file": "CONTEXT.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "context_degrees_per_count", "label": "0.06 Degrees Per Count", "file_type": "concept", "rationale": "4096 counts per servo turn through a 44:30 belt gives (360/4096)x(30/44) = 0.0599 degrees at the output.", "source_file": "CONTEXT.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "context_zero_deadband", "label": "Zero Deadband", "file_type": "concept", "rationale": "Measured landing error: 0 gives 0.06 deg, 1 gives 0.10, 8 gives 0.52, 32 gives 1.98.", "source_file": "CONTEXT.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "context_speed_saturation", "label": "Speed Saturates Near 1100 Counts/s", "file_type": "concept", "rationale": "About 66 deg/s at the output whatever is commanded; acceleration has no measurable effect above about 50.", "source_file": "CONTEXT.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "context_serial1_1mbps", "label": "Serial1 At 1 Mbps", "file_type": "concept", "rationale": "Bench-verified reliable: 200 of 200 reads at 220 microseconds.", "source_file": "CONTEXT.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "context_working_reference_first", "label": "Read The Working Reference Before Rewriting", "file_type": "rationale", "rationale": "Several bugs came from re-deriving solved behaviour instead of porting it.", "source_file": "CONTEXT.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}], "edges": [{"source": "context_ubiquitous_language", "target": "context_count", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "CONTEXT.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "context_ubiquitous_language", "target": "context_datum", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "CONTEXT.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "context_ubiquitous_language", "target": "context_snapshot", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "CONTEXT.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "context_ubiquitous_language", "target": "context_slot", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "CONTEXT.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "context_ubiquitous_language", "target": "docs_agents_domain_glossary_rule", "relation": "conceptually_related_to", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "sou